WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.175
This is Allen Company task training for crusher

00:07.175 --> 00:10.125
and plant workers. Shot rock goes into the primary

00:10.125 --> 00:13.213
hopper, a feeder sends it into the jaw crusher,

00:13.213 --> 00:15.838
conveyors carry it to screens that size it,

00:15.838 --> 00:18.312
oversize goes back through a cone crusher,

00:18.312 --> 00:20.637
and stackers build the finished piles.

00:20.637 --> 00:23.312
Every one of those machines has moving parts strong

00:23.312 --> 00:25.562
enough to pull you in and crush you,

00:25.562 --> 00:28.150
and most plant fatalities happen during cleanup

00:28.150 --> 00:30.375
or maintenance, not normal running.

00:31.500 --> 00:34.788
Inside the jaw, a moving jaw swings against a fixed

00:34.788 --> 00:38.025
one, driven by a heavy flywheel. The cone uses

00:38.025 --> 00:41.225
a gyrating mantle. Both keep storing energy after

00:41.225 --> 00:44.212
power is cut: a flywheel can keep turning,

00:44.212 --> 00:46.712
and a bridged rock can drop or kick out without

00:46.712 --> 00:47.438
warning.

00:50.758 --> 00:54.758
Gears, sprockets, chains, drive and tail pulleys,

00:54.758 --> 00:57.883
flywheels, couplings, shafts and belts,

00:57.883 --> 01:00.021
any moving part that could cause injury,

01:00.021 --> 01:02.796
is guarded. Guards must stay securely in place

01:02.796 --> 01:04.258
while the machine runs.

01:05.392 --> 01:09.317
Never reach over, under, around or through a guard.

01:09.317 --> 01:11.480
Guards are taken off only for maintenance with

01:11.480 --> 01:14.167
the equipment locked out, and they go back on before

01:14.167 --> 01:17.454
it runs. If you see a guard missing or damaged,

01:17.454 --> 01:18.342
report it.

01:21.686 --> 01:24.199
Before crushers or conveyors start,

01:24.199 --> 01:26.587
everyone who could be exposed gets warned.

01:26.587 --> 01:28.611
Where the whole conveyor can't be seen from the

01:28.611 --> 01:31.587
start point, there's an audible or visible warning

01:31.587 --> 01:34.811
system, with enough delay for people to get clear.

01:34.811 --> 01:37.011
When you hear that warning, get clear,

01:37.011 --> 01:39.311
and stay clear until you know it's safe.

01:40.436 --> 01:43.224
Know where every emergency stop and pull-cord is

01:43.224 --> 01:45.549
on your part of the plant. Learn them on your site

01:45.549 --> 01:48.861
tour. At Boonesboro: underground conveyors 1 through

01:48.861 --> 01:53.698
4, conveyors 2, 30, 31 and 32, and the front and

01:53.698 --> 01:57.423
shop fuel tanks. At Clover Bottom: the Liwell plant,

01:57.423 --> 02:01.111
primary, secondary, pug mill, surge tunnel and

02:01.111 --> 02:04.311
recycle bin. At Dix River, none of the conveyors

02:04.311 --> 02:06.974
have pull-cords or emergency stops;

02:06.974 --> 02:08.961
they're guarded by railings instead.

02:08.961 --> 02:11.586
Never reach or climb past a railing while a belt

02:11.586 --> 02:14.836
is running, and lock out before any work on a belt.

02:18.162 --> 02:20.625
Plant motors are fed from an electrical room,

02:20.625 --> 02:24.112
or MCC. Only qualified persons work inside the

02:24.112 --> 02:27.050
cabinets. What you need to know is which disconnect

02:27.050 --> 02:28.912
feeds the machine you're working on,

02:28.912 --> 02:30.188
so you can lock it out.

02:31.332 --> 02:34.345
Before cleanup, jam clearing or repairs,

02:34.345 --> 02:36.745
the machine is turned off, locked out with your

02:36.745 --> 02:39.632
own lock and tag, and blocked against motion.

02:39.632 --> 02:41.682
Then you try to start it to prove it's dead.

02:41.682 --> 02:44.732
Release stored energy: let flywheels stop,

02:44.732 --> 02:48.032
block material that could fall, relieve belt tension

02:48.032 --> 02:50.620
and hydraulic pressure. There's a full lockout

02:50.620 --> 02:53.945
lesson in the library; follow Allen's lockout procedure

02:53.945 --> 02:54.907
every time.

02:56.034 --> 02:58.834
When a rock bridges the jaw, never stand on the

02:58.834 --> 03:01.459
rock or in the crusher to bar it loose.

03:01.459 --> 03:04.634
At Allen, use the hydraulic rock breaker first,

03:04.634 --> 03:07.359
from a safe position. If that doesn't clear it,

03:07.359 --> 03:09.459
the crusher is locked out and blocked,

03:09.459 --> 03:11.934
and then the rock is moved with an excavator or

03:11.934 --> 03:14.509
blasted. Anyone working where there's a danger

03:14.509 --> 03:16.459
of falling is tied off.

03:17.580 --> 03:20.280
Don't clean pulleys or shovel under a running conveyor

03:20.280 --> 03:23.505
by hand. Belts pull in tools and arms faster than

03:23.505 --> 03:24.580
you can let go.

03:27.910 --> 03:30.835
Use the walkways, stairs and crossovers.

03:30.835 --> 03:33.622
Never crawl under or step over a conveyor.

03:33.622 --> 03:37.110
Keep walkways clear; housekeeping is a safety standard,

03:37.110 --> 03:38.085
not a chore.

03:39.208 --> 03:42.558
Nobody enters a bin, hopper or surge pile unless

03:42.558 --> 03:44.958
the supply and discharge are stopped and locked

03:44.958 --> 03:47.633
out, they wear a safety harness and line,

03:47.633 --> 03:49.870
and a second person is there to tend.

03:49.870 --> 03:52.445
Hung-up material can let go without warning.

03:55.778 --> 03:59.003
Crushers and screens are loud. At every Allen site,

03:59.003 --> 04:01.003
wear hearing protection around the plant while

04:01.003 --> 04:03.528
it's running and around the mine fans.

04:03.528 --> 04:06.690
Dust is controlled with water sprays and enclosures;

04:06.690 --> 04:09.778
report broken sprays. Our stone is very low in

04:09.778 --> 04:13.428
silica, but dust is still a respiratory irritant,

04:13.428 --> 04:15.840
so use the respirator where it's required.

04:15.840 --> 04:18.290
At every Allen site, that's outside the screen

04:18.290 --> 04:20.778
plant while it's running, and at Boonesboro also

04:20.778 --> 04:23.253
for certain shop and cleaning tasks.

04:26.580 --> 04:29.917
Recap: guards stay on; never reach through.

04:29.917 --> 04:32.280
Get clear when you hear the start-up warning.

04:32.280 --> 04:35.692
Lock out, tag out, block and try before cleanup

04:35.692 --> 04:38.830
or jams. No hand-cleaning moving pulleys.

04:38.830 --> 04:42.117
Use walkways and crossovers. Nobody enters a bin

04:42.117 --> 04:45.292
without lockout, a line and a tender.

04:45.292 --> 04:47.230
Protect your hearing and lungs.

04:48.342 --> 04:51.242
A competent person examines every working place

04:51.242 --> 04:54.529
each shift before work begins. If you find a hazard

04:54.529 --> 04:57.129
that wasn't caught, stop and report it.

04:58.248 --> 05:01.410
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

05:01.410 --> 05:02.910
override this video.
